<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2013/05/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>ktsu.Schema</id>
    <version>1.35.0</version>
    <title>ktsu.Schema</title>
    <authors>ktsu.dev contributors</authors>
    <license type="file">LICENSE.md</license>
    <licenseUrl>https://aka.ms/deprecateLicenseUrl</licenseUrl>
    <icon>icon.png</icon>
    <readme>README.md</readme>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/ktsu-dev/Schema</projectUrl>
    <description>A .NET library for defining, managing, and editing data structure schemas with a rich type system, type-safe identifiers, and polymorphic JSON serialization. Define structured data models programmatically or visually and serialize them to .schema.json files, providing a metadata foundation for code generation, data validation, and tooling that needs to reason about your data structures. Ships with an accompanying Dear ImGui desktop editor for visual schema authoring.</description>
    <releaseNotes>## v1.35.0 (minor)

Changes since v1.34.0:

- Bound the recent-files menu, and stop a test resolving a path two ways ([@Claude](https://github.com/Claude))
- Pin every arity a quantity's representation can have ([@Claude](https://github.com/Claude))
- Say what a vector quantity's bytes are [patch] ([@Claude](https://github.com/Claude))
- fix: port the &lt;compare&gt; generator fix from #191 ([@Claude](https://github.com/Claude))
- ci: move the UI suite under tests/ so the exclude actually matches it ([@Claude](https://github.com/Claude))
- test: keep the editor's frameless tests off the Linux-only rule ([@Claude](https://github.com/Claude))
- ci: name the editor UI suite Schema.Editor.UITests ([@Claude](https://github.com/Claude))
- Include &lt;compare&gt; in a generated semantic type [patch] ([@Claude](https://github.com/Claude))
- Construct a quantity default the way the vocabulary accepts it [patch] ([@Claude](https://github.com/Claude))
- Take the two SonarCloud findings ([@Claude](https://github.com/Claude))
- ci: adopt the consolidated .NET workflow [patch] ([@Claude](https://github.com/Claude))</releaseNotes>
    <copyright>Copyright (c) 2023-2026 ktsu-dev contributors</copyright>
    <tags>schema;data schema;type system;polymorphic serialization;json schema;schema editor;imgui;data modeling;code generation;dotnet;csharp</tags>
